ic sector. This central role is reinforced by CNPD's collaboration with the Ministério Público in implementing policies and enforcing rights related to data, and by its structural inclusion of CNMP and CNJ as seated sectors to manage fundamental rights governance [Data: Relationships (406); Entities (414, 417)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"CNJ and CNMP are paired within CNPD, occupying two seats\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Within CNPD's governance framework, CNJ and CNMP are paired sectors that together occupy two seats dedicated to fundamental rights governance. This pairing underscores a deliberate cross-sector balance between judiciary and public prosecution perspectives in high-level governance decisions, reinforcing the integration of fundamental rights considerations into CNPD's work [Data: Relationships (406, 418)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"CNJ's explicit role in safeguarding fundamental rights and data governance\",\n      \"explanation\": \"CNJ is described as Brazil's National Council of Justice, the judiciary’s oversight and governance body, with designated seats within CNPD. This places CNJ at the forefront of interpreting and safeguarding fundamental rights within CNPD's data governance framework, contributing to the overarching norms that guide data governance in the judiciary and related sectors [Data: Entities (417); Relationships (418)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"CNMP's governance role within CNPD\",\n      \"explanation\": \"CNMP, as part of Brazil's National Public Prosecutor's Office, participates in CNPD's governance as a sector represented across CNPD's framework. The relationship describing CNPD's governance reveals CNMP's cross-sector representation and its collaboration with CNJ to support rights-related governance, illustrating CNMP's integral role in policy implementation and rights enforcement within the data governance architecture [Data: Entities (414); Relationships (406)].\"\n    },\n    {\n     